Expected elements: present

Identity bar with a chain-targeted exit (`← aztec`), hash, `Partial`, stepping controls both directions, scrubber, `128 / 1315`, named phase rail; Code pane positioned at line 32; Call Trace and Event Log as one tab strip with Call Trace open above a separate Values pane; Transaction pane whose first labelled row is `Data`, badged `Synthetic demo data` with the producer's own sentences. No band above the identity bar, no prose band, no spinner, no explorer footer.

The copy is the strongest brand asset here: "Engine loading — 18 MB", "no call structure to trace", "This selector is not in any ABI BlockTracer holds… Supplying an ABI decodes them." Quantified, specific, never apologetic — this is the product's voice and it is intact in the light theme.

The register slips in one place, and consistently: the Transaction pane. Its label/value rows on hairline rules at ~30 px pitch, its proportional sentence-case paragraphs and its right-aligned `Data` block are the explorer's tx-detail overview docked to a debugger — a visitor arriving from `/tx/…` would not notice they crossed the boundary. Smaller: the Code pane opens with a sentence where the desktop app would draw a fold, and the same "this is selected" gesture is drawn three ways in one column.

Fixes: bring the Transaction pane to the density of Values — tighter rows, mono labels, left-set prose; unify the selection underline on one accent.

Rating: 7/10

